      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-12-19_WidnesExaminer_art0019" n="art0019">
        <head>DRESS-FASHION-HOME.</head>
        <p>DRESS-FASHION-HOME.</p>
        <p>THE Nzw JEWELLERY.'</p>
        <p>While the craze for enamelled jewellery ia 'thawing signs of being on the wane, a new vogue is springing up for every sort and description of what is best described as semi- precious jewels—a very different thing from the imitation article, but which, neverthe- less, are artistic rather than costly. First and foremost among novelties of this kind, says London Opinion, must be placed the beautiful new necklaces made in lovely colours of Venetian glass, threaded upon strands of gold Venetian beads. Not only are these ornaments extremely beautiful, being made in different colours, which include pale pink, a .lovely green like jade, deer, Indian red, and a perfect blue, but they have .he additional merit of being cheap.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-12-19_WidnesExaminer_art0020" n="art0020">
        <head>PEACOCK-BLUE COSTUME.</head>
        <p>PEACOCK-BLUE COSTUME.</p>
        <p>This smart costume is carried out in a deep shade of peacock-blue satin-faced cloth. The long clinging skirt has a narrow panel down the Centre of the front. The coat is three- quarter length, and the fronts and back are cut to points longer than the sides. The coat fits easily to the figure, and has just a slight short-waisted effect. _ It is trimmed on the shoulders and round the arms with fancy silk braid to match the colour of the material, ornaments of narrow braid b2ing placed at in.</p>
        <p>tervals round the curved edge of the v..ido braid. The braid is carried down the outside of. the sleeve and outlines the cuff, the nar- row braid ornaments trimming the lower part of the sleeve. There are three rows of braid round the basque ; and a row of cloth-covered buttons, attached to mitred tabs of braid, finish the fronts of the coat. The coat fastens with is little waistcoat of blue velvet, the col- lar being faced with the same material.</p>
