        <p>The wise mother always keeps a box of silver- wrapped Peps in the house at this time of the year when coughs, colds, and sore throat are particularly rife amongst old and young. If these ailments ate not checked at the onset by the Peps method, there is danger that serious throat trouble, chronic bronchitis or chest weakness in later life may bathe consequence. Mrs. Betsey Mindan, 02, Elizabeth-road, East Hato, London, E., says Peps proved a blessing in their home. She writes, " Our little gill, 31 years old, suffered a lot all last Winter from conOs and colds. At night she was restless and troubled with a dry hacking cough. We gave her several medicines, some 11me•made, with no good result. But by giving her Peps—a half-tablet at a time—her cough soon became less. Finding what an excellent medicine Peps were, we continued with them until the child was quite cured. 1 myself was troubled for months with a heavy cold which prevented me doing my ordinary wolk. Now, thanks, to Peps, I am quite well again. Peps also rid my husband of a nasty cold." " I find Peps very good for coughs and colds, and for invigorating and protecting the chest," writes Mrs. A. King, Lincoln Ball, Brighton, Norwich. "Oar little boy 4 years old, had influenza and a bad cough. I gave him some Peps and ha soon began to get better and is now quite well again. My husband and myself and the other children, all had influenza colds, and I had a bad cough besides, but we found Peps vety comforting and effectual. Peps warm-up the chest, and remove all coughing and soreness." Peps are invaluable for coughs, colds, bronchitis, influenza, croup, wheeziness, hoarseness, whooping cough, sore throat, etc. Of all chemists at Is. I.ld. or 2s. Od. a box. See the registered name, Peps, on every box, and refuse cheap and worthless substitutes.</p>
