        <p>TRAM FARES. agai The Chairman reported that the deputation appointed Mercury "), by the Parish Meeting to wait upon the Tramways P ntfls ben Committee with rer,ard to tram fares was listened to very patiently. They were told that the committee could not possibly see their way to drop the Lit-es to and from Stockton Heath, or to adopt Id. stages. No town, they said, had been able to prove that halfpenny stages would pay,i,</p>
