        <p>Aberdare Warrington Northern League Hull Kingston Rovers 2 4 36 A MONTII FOR ATTEMPTED SUICIDE. Lancashire BHalifaxarrow 3 5 21 At the Liverpool Sessions on Tuesday, William Clef? (30),f0r attempting to commit suicide by throwing himself under a train at Earlestown, on August 27th Swinton was sentenced to one month's imprisonment. It will Union Northern herert . be remembered that Claff jumped in front of a train at Tre -- Earlestown Station and sustained serious injuries to his hands and'arms.</p>
        <p>Abont 5,-606-4-ectra-t-o-rs WitnessCa-Ei keen and exciting struggle between these teams at Wilderspool on Satur- day. Gibbs kicked off, and Daintith early on checked the Wigan forwards, Mclntyre with a lofty kick soon gate the " Wirepullers" the advantage. Wigan were penalized and despite the extreme angle Mclntyre placed a goal. The visitors retaliated, and a determined raid led up to Creevey placing a goal from near the quarter line. Wigan continued to hold the upper hand and after Lees had checked another dangerous _raid, Warrington were once more penalised, and Creevey gave his side the lead with a fine goal from near half-way. I A useful run by Lees ought to have been turned to good account, and Wigr n were lucky to escape, Bradshaw being pulled up near the line. Another rally by Wigan resulted in Creevey placing his third goal, whilst near the interval a passing move- ment ended in Kerwin scoring at the corner and Creevey added a goal. Half-time: Wigan, four goals one try (eleven points) ; Warrington, one goal (two points). laming round the IVarringtonians played up splendidly, and %igen were generally on the defensive. The game was maintained at high pressure, and a brilliant passing bout led up to Bradshaw scoring far out, but Mclntyre made no mistake with the place kick. The Warrington forwards next exhibited some ' splendid footwork, and after Harmer and Belton had led the way in one dangerous rush, Foster went over with a try, but Mclntyre failed to give Lis side the lead from a somewhat easy position. Warrington were in a minority by a single point, but they attacked with grim ' deterreinatior and a penalty being awarded the home I side, Mclntyre placed a fine goal. Wigan had two unsuccessful shots in the last few minutes, and War- rington thus won a capital game by three goals two tries (twelve points) against four goals one try (eleven points).</p>
