        <p>THEFT OF AN OVERCOAT. At the Liverpool Sessions on Tuesday, Martin Moran (39), an umbrella maker, admitted having at Widnes on November 19th stolen an overcoat, the property of the Runcorn and Widnes Co-operative Society, Ltd. There were fifteen previous convictions against him.—Prisoner was now sentenced to twelve months' imprisonmcnt.</p>
