        <p>Would Not Break Stones. At the Borough Police Court, on Tuesday, Patrick Lee, an inmate of the Warrington Workhouse, was charged with neglecting to perform his task of break- ing stones.—Mr. J. F. Awhery, master of the Work- ] house, stated that prisoner had simply shirked his wolk through no cause whatever. He was a man of good physique and it was thought be might do some- thing for himself. He had been an inmate of the Union for three or four years.—Mr. John Constable I stated that prisoner bad 7 cwt. of steno to break in 1 one day but only broke 11 cwt. He simply shirked his task.—A man who had the same quantity of stones to break the previous day did V, cwt. in com- parison with prisoner's I cwt. He had been an inmate since 1902.—The Chief Constable stated that prisoner had been before the Coutt on one previous occasicn for refusing to perform his task and also for assaulting one of the porters at the Workhouse when be was sentenced to a month's imprisonment.— Defendant was sentenced to a month's hard labour.</p>
